    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0670" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg550"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Terres.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-12-09"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 726.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of Mr.
                    Powell’s No. 1874, of the 20th ultimo, in which he states that Mr. A. Lagojannis
                    is an American citizen, of Greek origin, and that he conducts a large retail
                    business in fancy articles. He adds that, under the terms of the law now being
                    enforced, no foreigners, “except in special cases,” are allowed to conduct
                    retail business.</p>
                <p>If Mr. Lagojannis’s case is one of the special cases excepted from the terms of
                    the law he may press his claim of right to do business.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
